@1051 = ~Telim'Gar~
@1052 = ~Dillpater~
@1052199 = ~Drinks a potion~
@1053 = ~Grod One-Eye~
@1054 = ~Welcome, adventurers. Congratulations on surviving all the previous challenges. And so we meet for the final act. Know that here, your power will be tested beyond anything you have faced so far in my challenges. That said, let the slaughter begin! Oh, before that, let me give you a piece of advice: do not use the portable portal here. Really, don't use it.~
@1055 = ~Welcome, adventurers. Congratulations on surviving all the previous challenges. And so we meet for the final act. And congratulations on defeating the anomaly. Your name will be inscribed in the pantheon of heroes. However, know that here, your power will be tested beyond anything you have faced so far in my challenges. So, let the slaughter begin! Oh, before that, let me give you a piece of advice: do not use the portable portal here. Really, don't use it.~
@1056 = ~Welcome, adventurers. Congratulations on surviving all the previous challenges. And congratulations on defeating the anomaly and the Paragon of Cow Vengeance. Your name will be inscribed in the pantheon of the illustrious. However, know that here, your power will be tested beyond anything you have faced so far in my challenges. So, let the slaughter begin! Oh, and let me give you two pieces of advice: do not use the portable portal here. That would be a bad idea. And do not use the Pulverizer on me. I created it, so you can bet I made sure it wouldn't affect me.~

/*
@1057 = ~You do not have me "in your power." I defeated all your pathetic "bosses"; you are no match for me.~
@1058 = ~Why talk so much? Let's get this over with.~
@1059 = ~The pantheon of victors? The one inscribed in the Antimaginium? The one with a name erased from it?~
@10510 = ~My name is the one that's missing. I'm not dead, and I have no place on a list of the dead.~
@10511 = ~What are you doing here, then?~
@10512 = ~I'm seeking power, what else? What I want is your mages' spellbook. What Telim'Gar wants is your warriors' bodies. And what Grod wants is to slaughter whoever remains and offer their souls to his master.~
*/

//Welcome text too formal. Needs reworking.

//Welcome text as soon as the heroes enter the area.


//Text when the heroes see Telim'Gar for the first time:
@1057 = ~Yes, that's right, I'm a golem. I know what you're thinking, but you're wrong: I'm not a golem; I'm a mage who transferred his soul into a golem. Most mages seek immortality through lichdom. Not me. Ending up as nothing more than a skull obsessed with souls? No, thank you. I chose instead to have the blacksmith create an indestructible golem, then transferred my soul into it. I must admit, the blacksmith outdid himself: this new body of mine is virtually invulnerable.~

@1058 = ~So, did you enjoy my challenges? When you have eternity ahead of you and no inclination toward world domination, you have to find ways to keep yourself occupied. And I'm quite proud of what I've accomplished. I've thoroughly enjoyed watching you make your way through my challenges. You should know, however, that you were lucky to be able to choose them one at a time. A few decades ago, there was only one entrance, one exit, and they all had to be completed in sequence. But almost no one ever made it to me, so I had to trim down my challenges to make them more manageable. Consider yourselves lucky to have attempted them at the right time.~

@1059 = ~Enough talk. All things must come to an end. Dillpater here wants your mages' spellbooks. I want your warriors' bodies to add to my collection. Grod, my faithful lieutenant, will delight in slaughtering every last one of you... By the way, if any of you wishes to remain here and assist me in welcoming worthy heroes, step forward now... No one? Very well... In that case... Let's finish this.~



//Spellbooks, spellbooks, and more spellbooks. You could read them all, if you weren't afraid of starving to death in the meantime.

@105090 = ~Dillpater, you just disintegrated a Curst!~
@105091 = ~So what?~
@105092 = ~You know perfectly well you're not supposed to...~
@105093 = ~Not supposed to what? Touch your precious little darlings? Hold back my power for the sake of your "collection"?~
@105094 = ~Yes, they...~
@105095 = ~I'm tired of your rules. They're powerful; they deserve to witness my power.~
@105096 = ~... Fine, do as you please.~

@1050100 = ~Dillpater...~
@1050101 = ~What now?~
@1050102 = ~You disintegrated another Curst!~
@1050103 = ~You just disintegrated Grod!~
@1050104 = ~... All right, that's enough.~

@1050200 = ~You there! You have my spellbook! Give it back!~
@1050201 = ~Your spellbook? Ah yes, it bears your name.~
@1050202 = ~Yes. So give it back. Now!~
@1050203 = ~If you insist.~ //and Dillpater creates a portal and disappears.
@1050204 = ~Absolutely not. I'm keeping it.~ //and Dillpater goes into RAGE mode

@1050300 = ~We told you not to use the portal. Twice.~ // Chuck Norris (always curt and direct)
@1050301 = ~And two times, you didn't listen. That's not very aware.~ // JCVD
@1050302 = ~The first warning was free.~ // Chuck Norris
@1050303 = ~The second... is the ultimate retribution.~ // JCVD
@1050304 = ~FU-SION!~
@1050305 = ~One time, I thought. And the universe had a bug. Life is 1+1=1. Me and Chuck, we're 1, but even more aware. And when you're 1 with the universe, you don't just win... you ARE the win. Just by looking at you... BANG. You die.~
@1050306 = ~Chuck Norris~
@1050307 = ~Jean-Claude Van Damme~
@1050308 = ~Jean Chuck Van Damrris~

@1050401 = ~Chain Contingency: 3x Abi-Dalzim's Horrid Wilting~
@1050402 = ~Contingency: Mislead~
@1050403 = ~Spell Sequencer: 3x Flame Arrow~
@1050404 = ~Minor Sequencer: 2x Melf's Acid Arrow~
@1050405 = ~Dillpater's Sequencer: 3x Rainbow Missile~

